    <sys:String x:Key="s.tab.scan">Read Quests (BETA)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.scan.title">Read your quests from the game</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.scan.desc">No need to enter quests one by one: the tracker reads the quest names on the in-game Tasks screen. You confirm the list, the quests become active and everything before them counts as done.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.scan.step1">Set the game language to English and run the game in Borderless or Windowed mode.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.scan.step2">In game, open the TASKS page and go to Side tasks, so your quest list is on screen.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.scan.step3">Press "Start scan" below and switch to the game: scroll the quest list slowly to the bottom. The scan stops by itself after the countdown, or press "Stop".</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.scan.step4">Come back to this page, untick anything read wrong and press "Apply".</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.scan.once1">Short list? Press</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.scan.once2">to read only what is on the screen right now (once per page).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.scan.startHint">Frames are only read while the game is in front. The scan stops by itself when the countdown ends, so it never keeps the PC busy.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.scan.clear">Clear</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.scan.safe">It only takes a picture of the screen: no reading the game's memory, no fake key presses. Pictures stay in memory and are never saved or sent anywhere.</sys:String>
