    <sys:String x:Key="s.gps.safe">The game itself writes your position into a screenshot's file name. The picture is never opened, no key is read, nothing is sent to the game.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.gps.title">Show my position on the map</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.gps.desc">Take a screenshot in raid and a map window shows where you are and which way you face, the path of your earlier screenshots, the exfils and your active quests' spots. The floor follows your height.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.gps.step1">Enter a raid. The map follows the raid's map (picked on "Entering a raid" or found by the double O); without a raid, pick the map in the map window.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.gps.step2">Take a screenshot with your in-game screenshot key. Any key you bound works: the app watches the screenshot folder, not the key.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.gps.step3">The map comes up with you on it. Wheel zooms, dragging looks around, ◎ centres on you again.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.gps.step4">Press Esc (or click the game): the map closes and the game gets the keyboard back. Take another screenshot when you want to see where you are.</sys:String>
