    <!-- Help & About page -->
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.tab">Help &amp; About</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.title">HELP &amp; ABOUT</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.about.title">ABOUT</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.about.name">EFT Quest Helper</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.about.desc">A quest tracker, goal planner and in-game overlay for Escape from Tarkov (PvP and PvE). Free and open source. It runs next to the game as a separate Windows app: it never reads or changes the game's memory, files or network traffic.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.about.version">Version</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.about.data">Quest data comes from the Escape from Tarkov Wiki and tarkov.dev; flea prices and maps from tarkov.dev; Goon reports from tarkov-goon-tracker.com.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.about.site">Website</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.about.github">Source code (GitHub)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.about.releases">All versions</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.about.issues">Report a bug / suggest a feature</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.about.disclaimer">Escape from Tarkov, trader names and logos are trademarks of Battlestate Games. This app is an unofficial, non-commercial fan project and is not affiliated with Battlestate Games.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.setup.title">SET UP FOR THE BEST RESULT</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.setup.desc">Do these once and the app does most of the work for you in raid.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.s1.t">1. Run the game Borderless or Windowed</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.s1.d">In Tarkov's graphics settings pick Borderless or Windowed. Windows cannot draw the overlay, the map or the flea search over exclusive fullscreen.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.s2.t">2. Pick your profile and PvP / PvE</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.s2.d">Top bar: each profile and each mode keeps its own progress. Quest requirements and levels differ in PvE, so pick the mode you really play.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.s3.t">3. Set the languages</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.s3.d">Top bar or Settings: the app language changes menus and buttons, the quest language changes quest names and objectives. Search works in both languages.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.s4.t">4. Enter your progress once</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.s4.d">Fastest: Read Quests (BETA) scans the in-game Tasks screen in 30 seconds. Or mark the quest you are on as active, or make it your goal in the Goal Planner: every earlier quest in its chain counts as done. A wrong click is one "Undo" away.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.s5.t">5. Game in English for screen reading</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.s5.d">Read Quests and the double O raid detection read English text with Windows OCR. They work best with the game in English at 1080p or higher.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.s6.t">6. Keep the auto raid detection on</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.s6.d">Entering a raid page, top (on by default). Press O twice in raid: the map and the raid time are set and the overlay shows that map's quests. Leave "Show the overlay in streams and recordings" off (default) if the overlay sits over the exfil list in the top-right corner.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.s7.t">7. Tune the overlay</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.s7.d">Settings → Overlay: how many quests it shows, hiding completed objectives, the detailed or the titles-only view, opacity and position. Ctrl + mouse wheel over the overlay sizes it, dragging its header moves it. Auto-hide shows it only when you press O in game.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.s8.t">8. Pin what you want to see</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.s8.d">Active Quests: turn on 📌 Overlay for the quests you want on the overlay outside a raid. In a raid the overlay shows that map's active quests by itself.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.s9.t">9. Set up the GPS map</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.s9.d">Bind a screenshot key in the game. If your screenshots are not in Documents\Escape from Tarkov\Screenshots, pick the folder on the In-Game GPS page. Then choose how the map shows: over the game, as a round mini map, or inside the app on a second monitor.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.s10.t">10. Learn the hotkeys</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.s10.d">Ctrl+Shift+T locks the overlay so clicks go to the game, Ctrl+Shift+R picks the raid map, Ctrl+Shift+F opens the flea price search. They are listed under Settings and at the bottom of the window. If one clashes with another program, the app warns you at start.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.s11.t">11. Updates and backups</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.s11.d">Keep "Check GitHub for a new version at start" on: a new version installs with one click. Settings → Export saves your progress to a file you can import on any PC.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.faq.title">FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.q1.q">Can I get banned for using this app?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.q1.a">The app never touches the game: no memory reading, no DLL injection, no game file or network access, no fake key or mouse input. The overlay is an ordinary transparent window, the hotkeys use the standard Windows hotkey API, and the screen reading features only look at a picture of the screen, like a screenshot tool.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.q2.q">Why can't I see the overlay in game?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.q2.a">Run the game Borderless or Windowed: nothing can be drawn over exclusive fullscreen. Also check that the overlay is not hidden (Ctrl+Shift+H), that auto-hide is off or that you pressed O, and that it has quests: pin some under Active Quests, or start a raid.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.q3.q">I can't click the game, the overlay takes my clicks.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.q3.a">Press Ctrl+Shift+T to lock the overlay: clicks then go straight through to the game. Press it again to unlock it and use its buttons.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.q4.q">Does the app track my quest progress by itself?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.q4.a">No, the game's memory and network traffic are never read, so you tick objectives yourself. What it does by itself: Read Quests imports your active quests from the Tasks screen, and the double O picks the raid map and time.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.q5.q">The double O does not start the raid.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.q5.a">Check that auto detection is on (Entering a raid page), the game is in English, and nothing covers the exfil list in the top-right corner. It needs an exfil that only that map has, so it waits when it is not sure. You can always pick the map with Ctrl+Shift+R.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.q6.q">The map does not show where I am.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.q6.a">Take a screenshot with the key you bound in the game: your position is in the file name. Make sure the GPS is on and the screenshot folder on the In-Game GPS page is the one the game saves to.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.q7.q">How do I update without losing my progress?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.q7.a">Use the Update button when a new version is found: progress stays. For a manual update, copy the data\profiles folder next to the exe into the new version, or use Export / Import in Settings.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.q8.q">Where is my data stored? Is anything sent anywhere?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.q8.a">Everything stays in the data folder next to the app. There is no account and no telemetry. The app only downloads public data: flea prices and maps from tarkov.dev, Goon reports, quest updates from the wiki and new versions from GitHub.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.q9.q">Can several people use it on one PC?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.q9.a">Yes. Create a profile for each player in the top bar: every profile has its own PvP and PvE progress, overlay settings, languages and hotkeys.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.q10.q">A quest is wrong or missing.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="s.help.q10.a">Settings → Data → "Update from wiki" refreshes the quests. If it is still wrong, report it on GitHub with the quest name.</sys:String>
</ResourceDictionary>
